{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["The sense of <b>ויהי ביום כלות משה</b>: after the priestly blessing, for so it was, for on the day Aaron lifted his hands toward the people and blessed them, the dedication of the altar began. And the verse 'ויהי ביום כלות משה להקים את המשכן' is on account of the words of the transmitters [of tradition], for he would dismantle it and set it up, and again dismantle it and set it up, all seven days of ordination, to accustom them. For the sense of 'ויקדש אותם' is by sprinkling the blood during the seven days of ordination." "<b>ואת המזבח ואת כל כליו.</b> Attached to 'ביום כלות משה להקים את המשכן,' and the sense is that he set up the altar in its place." "<b>ואת כל כליו וימשחם.</b> With the anointing oil." "<b>ויקדש אותם.</b> With blood. And he mentioned the altar on account of the dedication."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:42.820955886Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}